{
  "id": "ln9tnlx",
  "title": "Chapter 4: Input Devices",
  "order": 4,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "246orvk",
      "content": "Input devices are hardware components used to enter data, instructions, or commands into a computer system. They allow users to interact with the computer and provide the raw data that the computer processes."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Primary Device",
          "value": "Keyboard",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Pointing Device",
          "value": "Mouse",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Recognition Systems",
          "value": "OMR, OCR, MICR",
          "icon": "info"
        }
      ],
      "id": "m6et6ul"
    },
    {
      "id": "uwkyr4k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.1 Keyboard"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Keyboards and mice serve as the core manual input devices for user interaction.",
        "Scanners capture physical documents and convert them into digital formats.",
        "Barcode Readers quickly read encoded visual strip patterns for tracking and sales.",
        "Specialized recognition systems comprise OMR, OCR, and MICR for rapid data capture and processing."
      ],
      "id": "b9zagko"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3kkxd1m",
      "content": "A keyboard is the most commonly used input device. It is used to type text, numbers, and commands into the computer."
    },
    {
      "id": "bv6z0zv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4.1.1 Types of Keys"
    },
    {
      "id": "x6ryyqx",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Key Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Function</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Alphanumeric Keys</p>",
            "<p>Used for typing letters and numbers.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Function Keys (F1–F12)</p>",
            "<p>Used for special functions depending on the software.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Control Keys</p>",
            "<p>Keys such as Ctrl, Alt, Esc used for command operations.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Navigation Keys</p>",
            "<p>Arrow keys, Home, End used for moving the cursor.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Numeric Keypad</p>",
            "<p>Used for entering numbers quickly.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zc4xdcv",
      "content": "Important Exam Points:"
    },
    {
      "id": "9h3gnlt",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Keyboard is the primary input device.",
        "Standard keyboard has around 104 keys.",
        "Function keys are located at the top of the keyboard."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ub7tr0v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.2 Mouse"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7xt0i74",
      "content": "A mouse is a pointing device used to move the cursor on the computer screen and select objects."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Chapter 4: Input Devices",
      "id": "5nwdmi2"
    },
    {
      "id": "5i93cjf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4.2.1 Types of Mouse"
    },
    {
      "id": "e54gap9",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mechanical Mouse</p>",
            "<p>Uses a rubber ball to detect movement.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Optical Mouse</p>",
            "<p>Uses light sensors to detect movement.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Wireless Mouse</p>",
            "<p>Works without cable using Bluetooth or RF.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9kzc2pj",
      "content": "Common Mouse Operations:"
    },
    {
      "id": "fcmmuqh",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Click",
        "Double Click",
        "Right Click",
        "Drag and Drop",
        "Scroll"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "7kf610v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.3 Scanner"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sews4rd",
      "content": "A scanner is an input device used to convert physical documents or images into digital format."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Technology",
        "Full Name",
        "Primary Application"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "OMR",
          "Optical Mark Recognition",
          "Evaluating objective test answer sheets"
        ],
        [
          "OCR",
          "Optical Character Recognition",
          "Converting scanned text images into editable text"
        ],
        [
          "MICR",
          "Magnetic Ink Character Recognition",
          "Processing bank cheques using special magnetic ink"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "ged8rms"
    },
    {
      "id": "np0rycw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4.3.1 Types of Scanners"
    },
    {
      "id": "reh4oo4",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Scanner Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Flatbed Scanner</p>",
            "<p>Most common scanner used for documents and photos.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Handheld Scanner</p>",
            "<p>Portable scanner moved manually over the document.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Drum Scanner</p>",
            "<p>Used for high-quality image scanning in publishing.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "695xl2c",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.4 Barcode Reader"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3lv90w6",
      "content": "A barcode reader is an input device used to read barcodes printed on products. It converts barcode patterns into digital data."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cvt21nv",
      "content": "Common Uses:"
    },
    {
      "id": "e7p7sps",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Retail stores",
        "Inventory management",
        "Libraries",
        "Logistics tracking"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "88hpe69",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.5 OMR, OCR, MICR"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions frequently distinguish between OMR (Optical Mark Recognition), OCR (Optical Character Recognition), and MICR (Magnetic Ink Character Recognition).",
        "Be prepared for questions regarding key classifications (Function keys, Toggle keys, Modifier keys) on standard keyboards.",
        "Understand MICR application specifically in banking for processing cheques."
      ],
      "id": "o92psc8"
    },
    {
      "id": "xpqbhds",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Technology</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Full Form</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Usage</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>OMR</p>",
            "<p>Optical Mark Recognition</p>",
            "<p>Used for reading marked answers in exams.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>OCR</p>",
            "<p>Optical Character Recognition</p>",
            "<p>Converts printed text into editable digital text.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>MICR</p>",
            "<p>Magnetic Ink Character Recognition</p>",
            "<p>Used in banking to read cheque numbers.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "gpzo2p6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.6 Other Input Devices"
    },
    {
      "id": "c3qiw2g",
